ation rights was approximately $7.8 million.","context":"67","section":"Item 5.A. Management’s Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Operating Results","block":722,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001731122-26-000158","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-01-30","reportDate":"2025-09-30","cik":"0001979610","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1979610/000173112226000158/e7256_20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/96222b68f8b625ae5316a38ab17b19a427a1f2bab8a3cba1e5f7ccfeaf73d0b3.bin","sha256":"96222b68f8b625ae5316a38ab17b19a427a1f2bab8a3cba1e5f7ccfeaf73d0b3"}},{"id":"ded8f679649c324155a48077105ed33c64dede764b0d735f54df5ad8723ad761","quote":"Revenue from HVAC systems sales during the fiscal year ended September 30, 2025 decreased by approximately $6.9 million, or 89.5%, compared to the fiscal year ended September 30, 2024. The decrease is attributable to the following factors: (i) continued turbulence in global trade as well as declining consumer spending have constrained the expansion of China’s industrial production capacity, limiting our ability to secure incremental industrial construction projects; and (ii) a decline in the number of new real estate engagements obtained during this year, as the real estate developers adopted a more cautious stance with new investment.","context":"Revenue from sales of products","section":"Results of Operations","block":754,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001731122-26-000158","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-01-30","reportDate":"2025-09-30","cik":"0001979610","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1979610/000173112226000158/e7256_20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/96222b68f8b625ae5316a38ab17b19a427a1f2bab8a3cba1e5f7ccfeaf73d0b3.bin","sha256":"96222b68f8b625ae5316a38ab17b19a427a1f2bab8a3cba1e5f7ccfeaf73d0b3"}}],"omittedEvidenceCount"