948b0cd6df7f13c26fc5b0e28f9e2e5721a56279a9ea","quote":"In the past, shareholders of public companies have often brought securities class action suits against those companies following periods of instability in the market price of their securities. If we were involved in a class action suit, it could divert a significant amount of our management’s attention and other resources from our business and operations and require us to incur significant expenses to defend the suit, which could harm our results of operations. Any such class action suit, whether or not successful, could harm our reputation and restrict our ability to raise capital in the future. In addition, if a claim is successfully made against us, we may be required to pay significant damages, which could have a material adverse effect on our financial condition and results of operations.","context":"Any of these factors may result in large and sudden changes in the volume and price at which our ordinary shares will trade.","section":"● actual or anticipated fluctuations in our quarterly results of operations and changes or revisions of our expected results;","block":407,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001731122-26-000158","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-01-30","reportDate":"2025-09-30","cik":"0001979610","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1979610/000173112226000158/e7256_20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/96222b68f8b625ae5316a38ab17b19a427a1f2bab8a3cba1e5f7ccfeaf73d0b3.bin","sha256":"96222b68f8b625ae5316a38ab17b19a427a1f2bab8a3cba1e5f7ccfeaf73d0b3"}},{"id":"a01f8d3421d689a9cab9732717207d2804a8cf6cb9630e9942c32f56feae85b2","quote":"Certain recent initial public offerings of companies with public floats comparable to ours have experienced extreme volatility that was seemingly unrelated to the underlying performance of the respective company. We may experience similar volatility, which may make it difficult for prospective investors to assess the value of our ordinary shares.","context":"In the past, shareholders of public companies have often brought securities class action suits against those companies following periods of instability in the market price of their securities. If we were involved in a class action suit, it could divert a significant amount of our management’s attention and other resources from our business and operations and require us to incur significant expenses to defend the suit, which could harm our results of operations. Any such class action suit, whether or not successful, could harm our reputation and restrict our ability to raise capital in the future. In addition, if a claim is successfully made against us, we may be required to pay significant damages, which could have a material adverse effect on our financial condition and results of operations.","section":"● actual or anticipated fluctuations in our quarterly results of operations and changes or revisions of our expected results;","block":408,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001731122-26-000158","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-01-30","reportDate":"2025-09-30","cik":"0001979610","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1979610/000173112226000158/e7256_20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/96222b68f8b625ae5316a38ab17b19a427a1f2bab8a3cba1e5f7ccfeaf73d0b3.bin","sha256":"96222b68f8b625ae5316a38ab17b19a427a1f2bab8a3cba1e5f7ccfeaf73d0b3"}},{"id":"dad47655902c2a09a8248385704be5042b51d01b0bcf3788fc77f2cd31c0109e","quote":"In addition to the risks addressed above in “- The trading price of our ordinary shares may be volatile, which could result in substantial losses to investors”, our ordinary shares may be subject to extreme volatility that is seemingly unrelated to the underlying performance of our business. Recently, companies with comparable public floats and initial public offering sizes have experienced instances of extreme stock price run-ups followed by rapid price declines, and such stock price volatility was seemingly unrelated to the respective company’s underlying performance. Although the specific cause of such volatility is unclear, our public float may amplify the impact the actions taken by a few shareholders have on the price of our ordinary shares, which may cause our share price to deviate, potentially significantly, from a price that better reflects the underlying performance of our business. Should our ordinary shares experience run-ups and declines that are seemingly unrelated to our actual or expected operating performance and financial condition or prospects, prospective investors may have difficulty assessing the rapidly changing value of our ordinary shares. In addition, investors in our ordinary shares may experience losses, which may be material, if the price of our ordinary shares declines or if such investors purchase shares of our ordinary shares prior to any price decline.","context":"Certain recent initial public offerings of companies with public floats comparable to ours have experienced extreme volatility that was seemingly unrelated to the underlying performance of the respective company. We may experience similar volatility, which may make it difficult for prospective investors to assess the value of our ordinary shares.","section":"● actual or anticipated fluctuations in our quarterly results of operations and changes or revisions of our expected results;","block":409,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001731122-26-000158","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-01-30","reportDate":"2025-09-30","cik":"0001979610","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1979610/000173112226000158/e7256_20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/96222b68f8b625ae5316a38ab17b19a427a1f2bab8a3cba1e5f7ccfeaf73d0b3.bin","sha256":"96222b68f8b625ae5316a38ab17b19a427a1f2bab8a3cba1e5f7ccfeaf73d0b3"}},{"id":"50f5be284a2bb406ebdacbabc8e68b85903678165dd7f3b10b82b0f2332d8d8b","quote":"If securities or industry analysts do not publish research or reports about our business, or if they adversely change their recommendations regarding our ordinary shares, the market price for our ordinary shares and trading volume could decline.","context":"olatility that is seemingly unrelated to the underlying performance of our business. Recently, companies with comparable public floats and initial public offering sizes have experienced instances of extreme stock price run-ups followed by rapid price declines, and such stock price volatility was seemingly unrelated to the respective company’s underlying performance. Although the specific cause of such volatility is unclear, our public float may amplify the impact the actions taken by a few shareholders have on the price of our ordinary shares, which may cause our share price to deviate, potentially significantly, from a price that better reflects the underlying performance of our business. Should our ordinary shares experience run-ups and declines that are seemingly unrelated to our actual or expected operating performance and financial condition or prospects, prospective investors may have difficulty assessing the rapidly changing value of our ordinary shares. In addition, investors in our ordinary shares may experience losses, which may be material, if the price of our ordinary shares declines or if such investors purchase shares of our ordinary shares prior to any price decline.","section":"● actual or anticipated fluctuations in our quarterly results of operations and changes or revisions of our expected results;","block":410,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001731122-26-000158","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-01-30","reportDate":"2025-09-30","cik":"0001979610","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1979610/000173112226000158/e7256_20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/96222b68f8b625ae5316a38ab17b19a427a1f2bab8a3cba1e5f7ccfeaf73d0b3.bin","sha256":"96222b68f8b625ae5316a38ab17b19a427a1f2bab8a3cba1e5f7ccfeaf73d0b3"}},{"id":"026d145b92b674017f212375cc173482ce0f5fe347e6165beaa79d9549e88d90","quote":"The trading market for our ordinary shares will be influenced by research or reports that industry or securities analysts publish about our business. If one or more analysts who cover us downgrade our ordinary shares, the market price for our ordinary shares would likely decline. If one or more of these analysts cease to cover us or fail to regularly publish reports on us, we could lose visibility in the financial markets, which in turn could cause the market price or trading volume of our ordinary shares to decline.","context":"If securities or industry analysts do not publish research or reports about our business, or if they adversely change their recommendations regarding our ordinary shares, the market price for our ordinary shares and trading volume could decline.","section":"● actual or anticipated fluctuations in our quarterly results of operations and changes or revisions of our expected results;","block":411,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001731122-26-000158","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-01-30","reportDate":"2025-09-30","cik":"0001979610","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1979610/000173112226000158/e7256_20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/96222b68f8b625ae5316a38ab17b19a427a1f2bab8a3cba1e5f7ccfeaf73d0b3.bin","sha256":"96222b68f8b625ae5316a38ab17b19a427a1f2bab8a3cba1e5f7ccfeaf73d0b3"}},{"id":"2185e044383ce2f7d04b0d8cf41ab00059f979d5143f75626be351f12f95443f","quote":"The sale or availability for sale of substantial amounts of our ordinary shares could adversely affect their market price.","context":"The trading market for our ordinary shares will be influenced by research or reports that industry or 