ll be classified as a passive foreign investment company, which is known as a PFIC, for any taxable year if, for such year, either:","section":"● actual or anticipated fluctuations in our quarterly results of operations and changes or revisions of our expected results;","block":420,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001731122-26-000158","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-01-30","reportDate":"2025-09-30","cik":"0001979610","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1979610/000173112226000158/e7256_20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/96222b68f8b625ae5316a38ab17b19a427a1f2bab8a3cba1e5f7ccfeaf73d0b3.bin","sha256":"96222b68f8b625ae5316a38ab17b19a427a1f2bab8a3cba1e5f7ccfeaf73d0b3"}},{"id":"143274e46fe0b5924d188f9bf4c7cd985127e69fa9f161773fe2ddd647c34c36","quote":"● The average percentage of our assets (determined at the end of each quarter) during the taxable year which produces passive income or which are held for the production of passive income is at least 50%.","context":"● At least 75% of our gross income for the year is passive income; or","section":"● actual or anticipated fluctuations in our quarterly results of operations and changes or revisions of our expected results;","block":421,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001731122-26-000158","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-01-30","reportDate":"2025-09-30","cik":"0001979610","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1979610/000173112226000158/e7256_20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/96222b68f8b625ae5316a38ab17b19a427a1f2bab8a3cba1e5f7ccfeaf73d0b3.bin","sha256":"96222b68f8b625ae5316a38ab17b19a427a1f2bab8a3cba1e5f7ccfeaf73d0b3"}},{"id":"8be46db35de11fe4bb8dc85c0f88d51fb20a32ec5eba6dc087d4118eac3af657","quote":"Passive income generally includes dividends, interest, rents, royalties (other than rents or royalties derived from the active conduct of a trade or business) and gains from the disposition of passive assets.","context":"● The average percentage of our assets (determined at the end of each quarter) during the taxable year which produces passive income or which are held for the production of passive income is at least 50%.","section":"● actual or anticipated fluctuations in our quarterly results of operations and changes or revisions of our expected results;","block":422,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001731122-26-000158","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-01-30","reportDate":"2025-09-30","cik":"0001979610","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1979610/000173112226000158/e7256_20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/96222b68f8b625ae5316a38ab17b19a427a1f2bab8a3cba1e5f7ccfeaf73d0b3.bin","sha256":"96222b68f8b625ae5316a38ab17b19a427a1f2bab8a3cba1e5f7ccfeaf73d0b3"}},{"id":"4e93ede425fcfd6f5c59e745072cb9255661955dd5b1c88362728ef164a64bd1","quote":"If we are determined to be a PFIC for any taxable year (or portion thereof) that is included in the holding period of a U.S. taxpayer who holds our ordinary shares, the U.S. taxpayer may be subject to increased U.S. federal income tax liability and may be subject to additional reporting requirements.","context":"Passive income generally includes dividends, interest, rents, royalties (other than rents or royalties derived from the active conduct of a trade or business) and gains from the disposition of passive assets.","section":"● actual or anticipated fluctuations in our quarterly results of operations and changes or revisions of our expected results;","block":423,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001731122-26-000158","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-01-30","reportDate":"2025-09-30","cik":"0001979610","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1979610/000173112226000158/e7256_20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/96222b68f8b625ae5316a38ab17b19a427a1f2bab8a3cba1e5f7ccfeaf73d0b3.bin","sha256":"96222b68f8b625ae5316a38ab17b19a427a1f2bab8a3cba1e5f7ccfeaf73d0b3"}},{"id":"7701f4673148108bb2c05ed973c6e9c8bbead4c041a60f4cdbfbccf577e0fae8","quote":"Depending on the amount of cash we hold, together with any other assets held for the production of passive income, it is possible that, for our current taxable year or for any subsequent year, more than 50% of our assets may be assets which produce passive income. We will make this determination following the end of any particular tax year. Although the law in this regard is unclear, we treat our consolidated affiliated entities as being owned by us for United States federal income tax purposes, because we consolidate their operating results in our consolidated financial statements. For purposes of the PFIC analysis, in general, a non-U.S. corporation is deemed to own its pro rata share of the gross income and assets of any entity in which it is considered to own at least 25% of the equity by value.","context":"If we are determined to be a PFIC for any taxable year (or portion thereof) that is included in the holding period of a U.S. taxpayer who holds our ordinary shares, the U.S. taxpayer may be subject to increased U.S. federal income tax liability and may be subject to additional reporting requirements.","section":"● actual or anticipated fluctuations in our quarterly results of operations and changes or revisions of our expected results;","block":424,"table":null,"attribution":"management","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001731122-26-000158","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-01-30","reportDate":"2025-09-30","cik":"0001979610","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1979610/000173112226000158/e7256_20-f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/96222b68f8b625ae5316a38ab17b19a427a1f2bab8a3cba1e5f7ccfeaf73d0b3.bin","sha256":"96222b68f8b625ae5316a38ab17b19a427a1f2bab8a3cba1e5f7ccfeaf73d0b3"}}